Bugfix: Account no longer stops syncing after a redirected settings request

If the server answered the first request for the server capabilities with a
redirect, the client blocked its request queue to check the connection and
never released it again, because the request it waited for was in that queue.
The account looked connected but did not sync until the client was restarted.

The queue is released as soon as the connection check has passed. A request
that is still redirected after all retries now ends with an error and is tried
again with the next regular connection check.
